// Local dialogue does not use stock quest or player-ship flags.
{1}{If you're here for cargo, speak to its owner. If you're here for trouble, take it somewhere else.}{If you're here for cargo, speak to its owner. If you're here for trouble, take it somewhere else.}{}{}{}{}
{2}{Who runs this landing?}{}{5}{}{10}{}
{3}{Can I book passage on that ship?}{}{5}{}{20}{}
{4}{Where can I buy supplies?}{}{5}{}{30}{}
{5}{I'll leave you to it.}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{6}{Me need things.}{}{-4}{}{30}{}
{7}{Me go.}{}{-4}{}{0}{}
{10}{I mind the landing. Everyone else minds their own business. We take cargo from wherever there's money to be made, but that doesn't give visitors leave to help themselves.}{I mind the landing. Everyone else minds their own business. We take cargo from wherever there's money to be made, but that doesn't give visitors leave to help themselves.}{}{}{}{}
{11}{Another question.}{}{5}{}{1}{}
{12}{Fair enough.}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{20}{She's tied up for cargo. No passenger passage at present. The Distant Traveller by the approach can get you back where you came from.}{She's tied up for cargo. No passenger passage at present. The Distant Traveller by the approach can get you back where you came from.}{}{}{}{}
{21}{Another question.}{}{5}{}{1}{}
{22}{I'll speak to her.}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{30}{Marek, the Cove Trader, keeps a post near the entrance. If you've something to sell, take it to him.}{Marek, the Cove Trader, keeps a post near the entrance. If you've something to sell, take it to him.}{}{}{}{}
{31}{Another question.}{}{5}{}{1}{}
{32}{Thank you.}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{33}{Me find him.}{}{-4}{}{0}{}
